    "faq.sections.administration": "Administration",
    "faq.gettingStarted.signIn.question": "How do I sign in?",
    "faq.gettingStarted.signIn.answer": "Open the VstPBX web interface in your browser and enter your username and password. You will receive your credentials from your administrator.",
    "faq.gettingStarted.changePassword.question": "How do I change my password?",
    "faq.gettingStarted.changePassword.answer": "Click your username in the top right and choose “Change password”. Enter your current password and the new password. Admins can also change passwords under Settings → Users.",
    "faq.gettingStarted.dashboard.question": "What do I see on the dashboard?",
    "faq.gettingStarted.dashboard.answer": "The dashboard shows the current status of your extensions and trunks, the overall system status, and recent calls.",
    "faq.settingUpPhone.registration.question": "Which details do I need to register a phone?",
    "faq.settingUpPhone.registration.answer": "You need the SIP server (server IP), your extension number as the username, the SIP password, and port 5060 (UDP). You can find these in your welcome email or ask your administrator.",
    "faq.settingUpPhone.supportedDevices.question": "Which phones and softphones are supported?",
    "faq.settingUpPhone.supportedDevices.answer": "VstPBX is compatible with all SIP-capable devices. This includes hardware phones from Yealink, Snom, Grandstream, Poly, and others, as well as softphones such as MicroSIP (Windows), Linphone (all platforms), or Zoiper.",
    "faq.settingUpPhone.troubleshooting.question": "My phone will not register. What can I do?",
    "faq.settingUpPhone.troubleshooting.answer": "Check: 1) Are the SIP server, username, and password correct? 2) Is port 5060/UDP allowed through the firewall? 3) Does the dashboard show the extension as offline? Contact your administrator if the issue persists.",
    "faq.callsNumbers.inbound.question": "How do inbound calls work?",
    "faq.callsNumbers.inbound.answer": "Inbound calls are routed to your extension via the assigned numbers (DIDs). An extension can have multiple numbers, including numbers from different trunks.",
    "faq.callsNumbers.outbound.question": "How do outbound calls work?",
    "faq.callsNumbers.outbound.answer": "For outbound calls, the selected number is sent as the caller ID. If multiple numbers are assigned to an extension, you can choose the DID under Extension details → “Outbound number”. If none is selected, the first assigned number is used.",
    "faq.callsNumbers.history.question": "Where can I find the call history?",
    "faq.callsNumbers.history.answer": "Select “Call history” in the main menu to see inbound and outbound calls with their date, time, duration, and status. You can filter by source and destination number.",
    "faq.callsNumbers.pai.question": "What is P-Asserted-Identity (PAI)?",
    "faq.callsNumbers.pai.answer": "PAI is a SIP header that confirms the caller’s identity to the provider. For number blocks, many providers require the main number of the block to be sent as PAI. You can configure PAI for each extension under Extension details → “P-Asserted-Identity (PAI)”. The domain is taken from the trunk automatically.",
    "faq.callsNumbers.forwarding.question": "What is call forwarding and how do I set it up?",
    "faq.callsNumbers.forwarding.answer": "Call forwarding sends calls to another number when you are unavailable or cannot answer. Click your extension on the dashboard to configure forwarding.",
    "faq.administration.createExtension.question": "How do I create a new extension?",
    "faq.administration.createExtension.answer": "As an administrator, go to Settings → Users → “New user”. You can create an extension and assign numbers while creating the user.",
    "faq.administration.configureTrunk.question": "How do I configure a trunk?",
    "faq.administration.configureTrunk.answer": "Under Settings → Trunks, you can create and manage SIP trunks. Enter your provider credentials (server, username, and password) and define the number block.",
    "faq.administration.email.question": "How do I configure email delivery?",
    "faq.administration.email.answer": "Under Settings → Email, you can configure the SMTP server. It is used for welcome emails to new users and voicemail notifications.",
    "faq.administration.update.question": "How do I update VstPBX?",
    "faq.administration.update.answer": "The easiest way is through the web interface: Settings → Server → Update → “Install update”. Alternatively, connect via SSH and run: git pull origin main && docker compose up -d --build. Database migrations run automatically on startup.",
    "faq.administration.homeAssistant.question": "How do I connect VstPBX to Home Assistant?",
    "faq.administration.homeAssistant.answer": "Under Settings → Home Assistant, you can enable the integration. Enter the MQTT broker and generate an API key. VstPBX will then send call events via MQTT and provide sensors for extensions, trunks, and active calls.",
